+# Bun migration
+
+Requires Bun 1.4.4 (also pinned in CI and packageManager). Install with
+`bun install --frozen-lockfile`.
+
+- Run: `bun run run [name] [count]`, `bun src/main.ts [name] [count]`, or
+  `bash scripts/run.sh [name] [count]` (the shell launcher also works from other
+  working directories). The existing source and shell file modes are retained.
+- Check: `bun run typecheck`, `bun run check`, or `make check`. Native Bun checking
+  uses strict tsconfig settings and includes every TypeScript file under src,
+  including files not imported by the CLI. The @lib alias is shared by execution
+  and checking through tsconfig paths.
+- The original project had no tests, serve task, build task, assets, or runtime
+  dependencies. No replacement formatter or linter is introduced.
+
+Deno configuration and execution have been removed. Arguments, name trimming,
+JSON fields, environment values, and invalid-count stderr/exit status 2 are
+preserved. Bun automatic dotenv loading is disabled in bunfig.toml and explicitly
+in the CLI launch commands, preserving the original explicit environment behavior.
+The new development-only dependency @types/bun is pinned to 1.4.4; bun.lock records
+its resolved dependency graph. No existing dependency versions were replaced.
+
+Security difference: the old Deno command allowed environment access while
+restricting filesystem, network, and subprocess access by default. Bun does not
+provide that permission sandbox; the CLI has normal process permissions. Run it
+under OS/container isolation when handling untrusted code. The migrated CLI
+itself only reads arguments/environment and writes console output. Dependency
+lifecycle scripts have not been broadly enabled.
+
+Validation: baseline Deno strict checking passed. After migration, strict Bun
+checking and make check passed. Eight cases (defaults, trimmed/empty names,
+valid/invalid counts, and extra arguments) were compared against the Deno baseline
+through direct Bun, package script, and shell launcher: 24 matching outputs and
+exit statuses. A harmless .env fixture stayed unloaded through all three paths.
+An unimported source type-error probe was rejected, then removed. Clean frozen
+installation and checks were verified with Deno absent from PATH. Hosted GitHub
+Actions was updated but not executed remotely. Formatter/linter replacement and
+broad reformatting remain outside scope.
